-- title:
--   The full configuration weight vanishes outside the pattern
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be finite with decidable equality and let $H$ be an ordered pattern with positive top rank. Assume the top layer of $C$ refines the partition determined by $H$, and let $A$ be a closed atom configuration in $C$ whose witness is an occurrence of $H$. Then the full partial-configuration weight of $A$ is zero at every tuple that is not an occurrence of $H$.
